      "problem": "What is the diameter of a circle if its area is $\\frac{9}{25}\\pi ?$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of a circle is $A=\\pi {r}^{2}$, where $r$ is the radius. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{25}\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{9}{25}\\cancel{\\pi } & =\\cancel{\\pi }{r}^{2} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{25}} \\\\ r & =\\frac{3}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the diameter is\n\n$$\nd=2\\cdot r=2\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{6}{5}.\n$$",
